 "ratio_basis": "Geekbench 6 single-core: Ryzen 7 260 2451 (CPU-Monkey listing). No Zero 2 W Geekbench 6 entry was found; its RP3A0 is the Pi 3's BCM2837 Cortex-A53 at 1.0 GHz, so the Pi 3 Model B results (73 and 87 at 1.2 GHz, Geekbench browser 447040 and 8846649) and the Pi 3 B+ (118 at 1.4 GHz, 1252369) are scaled by clock to 61-84. The host-to-Pi ratio is then 29-40. Geekbench mixes in floating-point and vector work where the A53 falls further behind, while the detector is integer and memory bound, so the ratio is taken as an upper-to-lower bracket, not a point. Cross-check: PhotonVision users report 13-15 fps at 640 x 480 on a Pi 3B+ (Chief Delphi, 2023)",
