 "latency_basis": "Readout: the 2304 x 1296 mode runs at up to 56 fps, so a frame reads out in at most 1/56 s (rolling shutter; the frame's centre is half that after its first row). ISP and transfer to the ARM: one frame period at 30 Hz, an assumption (libcamera delivers a completed buffer after the ISP pass). Link: a 1 Mbaud UART message of about 40 bytes is 0.4 ms; 2 ms allows for scheduling, an assumption until phase E. Latency is counted from the middle of the exposure to the measurement arriving at the Teensy"
